    40	    new_solver_assumptions:
    41	      - each legend cell contains exactly one contiguous bottom-aligned vertical bar
    42	      - the beam footprint never overlaps two obstacle colors at once
    43	      - if a beam is already inside an obstacle due to pass-through, the next step cannot switch obstacle colors mid-block
    44	      - the main area is generated so that the intended paths do not cycle
    45	    generator_guards:
    46	      - all four obstacle colors appear in the legend
    47	      - east and west obstacle spans explicitly avoid the south lane so post-south turns exit instead of looping
    48	      - every candidate grid is validated against the fused solver and against alternate simulations
    49	  placement_legality:
    50	    - obstacle rectangles are chosen from non-overlapping edge-touching spans derived from the square position and obstacle thicknesses
    51	    - required span intervals guarantee each planned collision exists
    52	    - excluded span intervals prevent unintended repeat collisions that would create cycles or ambiguous traces
    53	    - the teal square is placed with a margin from all obstacles and boundaries, preserving clear beam corridors
    54	  visual_observability:
    55	    - the color quota is visible from bar height alone, with values restricted to 1..4 because the legend interior has four rows
    56	    - the turn direction is still readable from bar side
    57	    - the global turn cap is visible because one beam reliably dies on its third obstacle while another beam still turns on its second obstacle
    58	    - the generator rejects any sample where the fused output matches the source logic, the quota-only logic, or the turn-cap-only logic
    59	  neatness_and_inferability:
    60	    - the layout stays close to the original sparse edge-bar style, so the new behavior is carried by path differences rather than clutter
    61	    - color changes are not used as hidden indices; only geometry and visible legend tokens matter
    62	    - each accepted sample contains repeated evidence for the south obstacle's quota rule, making the multi-counter interaction inferable from few examples
    63	"""
    64	
    65	import random
    66	
    67	import numpy as np
    68	
    69	from arc_utils import bbox_coords, components_mask
